 ((48
  ("COMPUTER SECURITY INCIDENT HANDLING GUIDE" 0.58678 0.88244 0.04578 0.05845 0.05791 0.0098 0.00316 0.3183 0.0676 "Arial" 0.0088 nil nil 0 "Arial" nil)
  ("39" 0.49106 0.5091 0.93891 0.95434 0.95434 0.01543 0.00451 0.0000 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (" What additional tools or resources are needed to detect, analyze, and mitigate future incidents?" 0.11769 0.82834 0.09106 0.1065 0.1065 0.01543 0.00451 0.3345 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "ABCDEE+Webdings" nil)
  ("Small incidents need limited post-incident analysis, with the exception of incidents performed through" 0.11769 0.85392 0.11836 0.13379 0.13379 0.01543 0.00451 0.3028 0.0418 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("new attack methods that are of widespread concern and interest. After serious attacks have occurred, it is" 0.11769 0.87149 0.13442 0.14985 0.14985 0.01543 0.00451 0.2913 0.0301 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("usually worthwhile to hold post-mortem meetings that cross team and organizational boundaries to" 0.11769 0.82848 0.15033 0.16576 0.16576 0.01543 0.00451 0.3164 0.0521 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("provide a mechanism for information sharing. The primary consideration in holding such meetings is" 0.11769 0.8446 0.16639 0.18182 0.18182 0.01543 0.00451 0.3116 0.0550 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("ensuring that the right people are involved. Not only is it important to invite people who have been" 0.11769 0.82876 0.1823 0.19773 0.19773 0.01543 0.00451 0.3033 0.0621 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("involved in the incident that is being analyzed, but also it is wise to consider who should be invited for the" 0.11769 0.88177 0.19821 0.21364 0.21364 0.01543 0.00451 0.2946 0.0629 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("purpose of facilitating future cooperation." 0.11769 0.41773 0.21427 0.2297 0.2297 0.01543 0.00451 0.2531 0.0570 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("The success of such meetings also depends on the agenda. Collecting input about expectations and needs" 0.11769 0.87166 0.24533 0.26076 0.26076 0.01543 0.00451 0.2641 0.0282 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("(including suggested topics to cover) from participants before the meeting increases the likelihood that the" 0.11769 0.88217 0.26139 0.27682 0.27682 0.01543 0.00451 0.2782 0.0741 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("participants’ needs will be met. In addition, establishing rules of order before or during the start of a" 0.11769 0.83706 0.2773 0.29273 0.29273 0.01543 0.00451 0.2877 0.0899 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("meeting can minimize confusion and discord. Having one or more moderators who are skilled in group" 0.11769 0.85842 0.29321 0.30864 0.30864 0.01543 0.00451 0.3191 0.0580 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("facilitation can yield a high payoff. Finally, it is also important to document the major points of" 0.11769 0.80351 0.30927 0.3247 0.3247 0.01543 0.00451 0.3178 0.0780 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("agreement and action items and to communicate them to parties who could not attend the meeting." 0.11769 0.82565 0.32522 0.34065 0.34065 0.01543 0.00451 0.3376 0.0747 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Lessons learned meetings provide other benefits. Reports from these meetings are good material for" 0.11769 0.83549 0.35643 0.37186 0.37186 0.01543 0.00451 0.3019 0.0580 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("training new team members by showing them how more experienced team members respond to incidents." 0.11769 0.8778 0.37234 0.38777 0.38777 0.01543 0.00451 0.3367 0.0560 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Updating incident response policies and procedures is another important part of the lessons learned" 0.11769 0.82985 0.3884 0.40383 0.40383 0.01543 0.00451 0.2695 0.0670 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("process. Post-mortem analysis of the way an incident was handled will often reveal a missing step or an" 0.11769 0.86329 0.40431 0.41974 0.41974 0.01543 0.00451 0.3176 0.0586 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("inaccuracy in a procedure, providing impetus for change. Because of the changing nature of information" 0.11769 0.86734 0.42022 0.43565 0.43565 0.01543 0.00451 0.2743 0.0780 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("technology and changes in personnel, the incident response team should review all related documentation" 0.11769 0.87614 0.43628 0.45171 0.45171 0.01543 0.00451 0.2800 0.0799 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("and procedures for handling incidents at designated intervals." 0.11769 0.55878 0.45219 0.46762 0.46762 0.01543 0.00451 0.2440 0.0261 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Another important post-incident activity is creating a follow-up report for each incident, which can be" 0.11769 0.85094 0.4834 0.49883 0.49883 0.01543 0.00451 0.3037 0.0589 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("quite valuable for future use. The report provides a reference that can be used to assist in handling similar" 0.11769 0.87685 0.49931 0.51474 0.51474 0.01543 0.00451 0.2743 0.0360 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("incidents. Creating a formal chronology of events (including timestamped information such as log data" 0.11769 0.85731 0.51522 0.53065 0.53065 0.01543 0.00451 0.3045 0.0695 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("from systems) is important for legal reasons, as is creating a monetary estimate of the amount of damage" 0.11769 0.86978 0.53128 0.54671 0.54671 0.01543 0.00451 0.3339 0.0352 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("the incident caused. This estimate may become the basis for subsequent prosecution activity by entities" 0.11769 0.85912 0.54721 0.56264 0.56264 0.01543 0.00451 0.2921 0.0221 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("such as the U.S. Attorney General’s office. Follow-up reports should be kept for a period of time as" 0.11769 0.83356 0.56327 0.57871 0.57871 0.01543 0.00451 0.3150 0.0331 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("specified in record retention policies.^{45}" 0.11769 0.39616 0.57741 0.59461 0.59461 0.01543 0.00451 0.2541 0.0650 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (#("3.4.2 Using Collected Incident Data" 0 35 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.11769 0.43032 0.6102 0.62574 0.62574 0.01554 0.00501 0.3608 0.0402 "Arial,Bold" 0.0139 t nil 0 "Arial,Bold" t)
  ("Lessons learned activities should produce a set of objective and subjective data regarding each incident." 0.11769 0.86364 0.64146 0.65689 0.65689 0.01543 0.00451 0.2492 0.0580 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Over time, the collected incident data should be useful in several capacities. The data, particularly the" 0.11769 0.84866 0.65737 0.6728 0.6728 0.01543 0.00451 0.2883 0.0358 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("total hours of involvement and the cost, may be used to justify additional funding of the incident response" 0.11769 0.87856 0.67343 0.68886 0.68886 0.01543 0.00451 0.2894 0.0320 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("team. A study of incident characteristics may indicate systemic security weaknesses and threats, as well" 0.11769 0.86358 0.68934 0.70477 0.70477 0.01543 0.00451 0.3117 0.0394 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("as changes in incident trends. This data can be put back into the risk assessment process, ultimately" 0.11769 0.83172 0.70524 0.72068 0.72068 0.01543 0.00451 0.2859 0.0150 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("leading to the selection and implementation of additional controls. Another good use of the data is" 0.11769 0.82372 0.7213 0.73674 0.73674 0.01543 0.00451 0.3016 0.0531 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("measuring the success of the incident response team. If incident data is collected and stored properly, it" 0.11769 0.85944 0.73721 0.75264 0.75264 0.01543 0.00451 0.2823 0.0750 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("should provide several measures of the success (or at least the activities) of the incident response team." 0.11769 0.85764 0.75331 0.76874 0.76874 0.01543 0.00451 0.2752 0.0480 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Incident data can also be collected to determine if a change to incident response capabilities causes a" 0.11769 0.84133 0.76922 0.78465 0.78465 0.01543 0.00451 0.2646 0.0589 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("corresponding change in the team’s performance (e.g., improvements in efficiency, reductions in costs)." 0.11769 0.86502 0.78513 0.80056 0.80056 0.01543 0.00451 0.2980 0.1031 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Furthermore, organizations that are required to report incident information will need to collect the" 0.11769 0.8214 0.80119 0.81662 0.81662 0.01543 0.00451 0.3020 0.0944 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("                                                     " nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil)
  ("45" 0.11769 0.12749 0.8555 0.86388 0.86388 0.00839 0.00368 0.1230 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0076 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (#("General Records Schedule (GRS) 24, Information Technology Operations and Management Records, specifies that" 35 91 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.1471 0.82588 0.85712 0.8697 0.8697 0.01258 0.00368 0.2975 0.0464 "Times New Roman,Italic" 0.0114 nil t 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("“computer security incident handling, reporting and follow-up records” should be destroyed “3 years after all necessary" 0.1471 0.85009 0.87015 0.88273 0.88273 0.01258 0.00368 0.2654 0.0620 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("follow-up actions have been completed.” GRS 24 is available from the National Archives and Records Administration at" 0.1471 0.85775 0.88333 0.89591 0.89591 0.01258 0.00368 0.3250 0.0579 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("http://www.archives.gov/records-mgmt/grs/grs24.html." 0.1471 0.47219 0.89636 0.90894 0.90894 0.01258 0.00368 0.3447 0.3251 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil))
  (49
  ("COMPUTER SECURITY INCIDENT HANDLING GUIDE" 0.58678 0.88244 0.04578 0.05845 0.05791 0.0098 0.00316 0.3183 0.0676 "Arial" 0.0088 nil nil 0 "Arial" nil)
  ("40" 0.49106 0.5091 0.93891 0.95434 0.95434 0.01543 0.00451 0.0000 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("necessary data to meet their requirements. See Section 4 for additional information on sharing incident" 0.11769 0.85582 0.09106 0.1065 0.1065 0.01543 0.00451 0.2945 0.0700 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("data with other organizations." 0.11769 0.33123 0.107 0.12243 0.12243 0.01543 0.00451 0.2878 0.0301 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Organizations should focus on collecting data that is actionable, rather than collecting data simply" 0.11769 0.82225 0.13821 0.15364 0.15364 0.01543 0.00451 0.2832 0.1009 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("because it is available. For example, counting the number of precursor port scans that occur each week" 0.11769 0.85616 0.15412 0.16955 0.16955 0.01543 0.00451 0.2846 0.0570 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("and producing a chart at the end of the year that shows port scans increased by eight percent is not very" 0.11769 0.86073 0.17018 0.18561 0.18561 0.01543 0.00451 0.2676 0.0261 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("helpful and may be quite time-consuming. Absolute numbers are not informative—understanding how" 0.11769 0.85547 0.18609 0.20152 0.20152 0.01543 0.00451 0.3385 0.0510 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("they represent threats to the business processes of the organization is what matters. Organizations should" 0.11769 0.87119 0.202 0.21743 0.21743 0.01543 0.00451 0.2783 0.0311 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("decide what incident data to collect based on reporting requirements and on the expected return on" 0.11769 0.82602 0.21806 0.23349 0.23349 0.01543 0.00451 0.2758 0.0470 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("investment from the data (e.g., identifying a new threat and mitigating the related vulnerabilities before" 0.11769 0.85962 0.23397 0.2494 0.2494 0.01543 0.00451 0.3137 0.0789 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("they can be exploited.) Possible metrics for incident-related data include:" 0.11769 0.64297 0.25003 0.26546 0.26546 0.01543 0.00451 0.2756 0.0311 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (#(" Number of Incidents Handled.^{46} Handling more incidents is not necessarily better—for example," 2 30 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.11769 0.85714 0.27932 0.29652 0.29652 0.01543 0.00451 0.3691 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "ABCDEE+Webdings" nil)
  ("the number of incidents handled may decrease because of better network and host security controls," 0.1471 0.86318 0.297 0.31243 0.31243 0.01543 0.00451 0.2783 0.0221 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("not because of negligence by the incident response team. The number of incidents handled is best" 0.1471 0.84795 0.31306 0.32849 0.32849 0.01543 0.00451 0.2787 0.0231 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("taken as a measure of the relative amount of work that the incident response team had to perform, not" 0.1471 0.87603 0.32901 0.34444 0.34444 0.01543 0.00451 0.3159 0.0390 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("as a measure of the quality of the team, unless it is considered in the context of other measures that" 0.1471 0.85796 0.34507 0.3605 0.3605 0.01543 0.00451 0.3049 0.0150 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("collectively give an indication of work quality. It is more effective to produce separate incident" 0.1471 0.83145 0.36098 0.37641 0.37641 0.01543 0.00451 0.2851 0.0840 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("counts for each incident category. Subcategories also can be used to provide more information. For" 0.1471 0.86008 0.37704 0.39247 0.39247 0.01543 0.00451 0.2777 0.0470 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("example, a growing number of incidents performed by insiders could prompt stronger policy" 0.1471 0.81341 0.39295 0.40838 0.40838 0.01543 0.00451 0.3071 0.0654 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("provisions concerning background investigations for personnel and misuse of computing resources" 0.1471 0.85752 0.40886 0.42429 0.42429 0.01543 0.00451 0.2571 0.0750 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("and stronger security controls on internal networks (e.g., deploying intrusion detection software to" 0.1471 0.85374 0.42492 0.44035 0.44035 0.01543 0.00451 0.2785 0.0261 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("more internal networks and hosts)." 0.1471 0.39636 0.44082 0.45626 0.45626 0.01543 0.00451 0.3082 0.0368 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (#(" Time Per Incident. For each incident, time can be measured in several ways:" 2 21 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.11769 0.70598 0.46825 0.48368 0.48368 0.01543 0.00451 0.3562 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "ABCDEE+Webdings" nil)
  ("– Total amount of labor spent working on the incident" 0.1471 0.55177 0.49565 0.51243 0.51243 0.01543 0.00451 0.3662 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– Elapsed time from the beginning of the incident to incident discovery, to the initial impact" 0.1471 0.82525 0.52414 0.54091 0.54091 0.01543 0.00451 0.3571 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("assessment, and to each stage of the incident handling process (e.g., containment, recovery)" 0.1765 0.8349 0.54115 0.55658 0.55658 0.01543 0.00451 0.2803 0.0845 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– How long it took the incident response team to respond to the initial report of the incident" 0.1471 0.82119 0.56871 0.58548 0.58548 0.01543 0.00451 0.3524 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– How long it took to report the incident to management and, if necessary, appropriate external" 0.1471 0.84625 0.59719 0.61397 0.61397 0.01543 0.00451 0.3454 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("entities (e.g., US-CERT)." 0.1765 0.35922 0.61418 0.62961 0.62961 0.01543 0.00451 0.3795 0.0521 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  (#(" Objective Assessment of Each Incident. The response to an incident that has been resolved can be" 2 41 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.11769 0.86593 0.64161 0.65704 0.65704 0.01543 0.00451 0.3230 0.0180 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "ABCDEE+Webdings" nil)
  ("analyzed to determine how effective it was. The following are examples of performing an objective" 0.1471 0.86244 0.65752 0.67295 0.67295 0.01543 0.00451 0.3168 0.0639 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("assessment of an incident:" 0.1471 0.33536 0.67343 0.68886 0.68886 0.01543 0.00451 0.2876 0.0799 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– Reviewing logs, forms, reports, and other incident documentation for adherence to established" 0.1471 0.85422 0.70098 0.71776 0.71776 0.01543 0.00451 0.3325 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("incident response policies and procedures" 0.1765 0.47608 0.71797 0.7334 0.7334 0.01543 0.00451 0.2246 0.0579 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– Identifying which precursors and indicators of the incident were recorded to determine how" 0.1471 0.83545 0.74538 0.76215 0.76215 0.01543 0.00451 0.3305 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("effectively the incident was logged and identified" 0.1765 0.53217 0.76255 0.77799 0.77799 0.01543 0.00451 0.2747 0.0770 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("– Determining if the incident caused damage before it was detected" 0.1471 0.64706 0.78996 0.80673 0.80673 0.01543 0.00451 0.3604 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("                                                     " nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil nil)
  ("46" 0.11769 0.12749 0.82944 0.83782 0.83782 0.00839 0.00368 0.1230 0.0098 "Times New Roman" 0.0076 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("Metrics such as the number of incidents handled are generally not of value in a comparison of multiple organizations" 0.1471 0.83457 0.83106 0.84364 0.84364 0.01258 0.00368 0.3093 0.0449 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("because each organization is likely to have defined key terms differently. For example, most organizations define “incident”" 0.1471 0.87764 0.84409 0.85667 0.85667 0.01258 0.00368 0.2838 0.0465 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("in terms of their own policies and practices, and what one organization considers a single incident may be considered" 0.1471 0.83651 0.85712 0.8697 0.8697 0.01258 0.00368 0.2930 0.0114 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("multiple incidents by others. More specific metrics, such as the number of port scans, are also of little value in" 0.1471 0.79502 0.87015 0.88273 0.88273 0.01258 0.00368 0.3231 0.0490 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("organizational comparisons. For example, it is highly unlikely that different security systems, such as network intrusion" 0.1471 0.85134 0.88333 0.89591 0.89591 0.01258 0.00368 0.3013 0.0842 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil)
  ("detection sensors, would all use the same criteria in labeling activity as a port scan." 0.1471 0.63527 0.89636 0.90894 0.90894 0.01258 0.00368 0.2924 0.0540 "Times New Roman" 0.0114 nil nil 0 "Times New Roman" nil))
